# bibtool

Python 3.13+ CLI under `src/bibtool/`. Stdlib only — no third-party runtime deps.

## Modules

- `cli.py` — argparse, I/O, confirmation prompts
- `inspire.py` — INSPIRE HEP HTTP client, search/lookup, caches
- `bibtex.py` — parse/write/merge/dedupe BibTeX

Inject `InspireClient` (or stubs) via `run(..., provider=...)` in tests. Prefer `unittest`.

## Data source

Literature metadata comes from **INSPIRE HEP only** (`inspirehep.net/api/literature`).

- Do **not** call the arXiv API (rate limits / stalls).
- arXiv IDs, DOIs, journal data: take from INSPIRE JSON fields (`arxiv_eprints`, `dois`, `publication_info`, etc.) already returned with search/fetch.
- Prefer published INSPIRE records over preprint-only when choosing a match.

## Bibliography behavior

- Deduplicate case-insensitively by **title / DOI / eprint**, not BibTeX key.
- On match: update fields in place; **preserve existing keys**.
- New keys: `FirstAuthorYearFirstTwoTitleWords`.
- arXiv-only `@article`: set `journal = {arXiv}` for REVTeX/APS.
- Sort output by year, then first author, then title.
- `search`/`import` share `resolve_lookup` — keep search and fetch query/matcher parity.
- Search: loose INSPIRE keyword query, then local case-insensitive AND filter on metadata.
- Year tokens (`19xx`/`20xx`) in free-text query → INSPIRE `date:YYYY` + local year match.

## CLI

- Default import/update target: `$LATEX_TEMPLATE_DIR/references.bib` (override with path/`--bib`).
- Large imports (>10 entries): require double confirm unless `--y`.
- `update` never prompts; may parallelize with `--workers`.
- `download` mirrors `search` query flags; writes arXiv PDFs to `--dir` (default `.`); large batches need `--y` or double confirm.
- `download` accepts arXiv / INSPIRE ids (positional or `--arxiv` / `--inspire`).
- Do not call the arXiv API; PDF downloads use static `arxiv.org/pdf/{eprint}` URLs from INSPIRE eprint ids.
## Tests

```bash
python -m unittest discover -s tests
```

Clear INSPIRE response caches between tests that hit HTTP helpers (`clear_response_caches`).

See `ship-changes.mdc`: new behavior → unit tests → full suite green → commit + push.
